From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 12:26:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] spectro: fix Nutanix review findings in the conversion path

- virt-v2v: order mounted disks by index before matching them to the
  domain XML. filepath.Glob sorts lexically (disk10 before disk2) and
  file and block disks were globbed separately, so with 11+ disks, or a
  mix of filesystem and block PVCs, UpdateDiskPaths pointed XML disks at
  the wrong volumes.
- Nutanix domain XML: give IDE disks an hd* target. libvirt rejects sd*
  names on the ide bus.
- Nutanix static IPs: set V2V_multipleIPsPerNic when a preserved NIC has
  more than one static IP, as the vSphere and Hyper-V builders do, so the
  extra addresses are restored on Windows guests.
- Docs: insecureSkipVerify now also skips verification for disk
  transfers (spec.source.http.insecureSkipVerify, CDI >= v1.66).

Resolves: None

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
